{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Atx4x8vtnhV4xbLyBHpCVc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Intervals.icu API OAuth scopes ACTIVITY:READ CALENDAR:WRITE WELLNESS:READ refresh token expires_in\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu OAuth support\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759\"},{\"title\":\"Überauth intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://readme.hex.pm/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.0\"},{\"title\":\"Refresh the Access Token\",\"url\":\"https://www.manageengine.com/appcreator/help/api/v2/refresh-the-access-token.html\"},{\"title\":\"docs.treedis.com\",\"url\":\"https://docs.treedis.com/reference/models/OAuth2TokenData\"},{\"title\":\"OAuth Token Refresh\",\"url\":\"https://developers.hellosign.com/docs/guides/o-auth/token-refresh\"},{\"title\":\"docs.privy.io\",\"url\":\"https://docs.privy.io/reference/sdk/expo/interfaces/OAuthTokens\"},{\"title\":\"Name | Type | Description | Notes |\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/UltraCart/rest_api_v2_sdk_php/blob/a5e19d4d9bff2beb9b827077fc3da23902e38fb2/docs/Model/OauthTokenResponse.md\"},{\"title\":\"Using Refresh Tokens\",\"url\":\"https://docs.oracle.com/cd/F88966_01/English/Integration_Documentation/rest_api/D102899.html\"},{\"title\":\"Refresh the Access Token\",\"url\":\"https://prezohoweb.zoho.com/creator/help/api/v2.1/refresh-the-access-token.html\"}]\n\nThe search turned up two Intervals.icu sources that address your question, and they don't fully agree on token expiry.\n\n- **Official forum post:** Scopes are ACTIVITY, WELLNESS, CALENDAR, CHATS, LIBRARY, and SETTINGS. Each needs READ or WRITE, and WRITE implies READ. The token exchange response includes an access token, granted scopes, and the athlete's id and name. That sample response has no `expires_in` or `refresh_token` field, and the post doesn't say anything about expiry.\n- **Community Ueberauth integration docs (hex.pm):** This source says the service departs from typical OAuth. Tokens do not expire, and there are no refresh tokens. It also describes CALENDAR as covering planned workouts and calendar events, and it describes WELLNESS as covering weight, HRV, resting HR, and sleep. Its default scope list is inconsistent: one passage gives ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:WRITE and another gives ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ.\n\nThe other results were about unrelated OAuth providers (ManageEngine, Zoho, Oracle, Treedis, HelloSign), so I've left them out. I found nothing confirming a `CALENDAR:WRITE` scope string as written, though the forum's scope format implies it is valid. I'd check the official Intervals.icu API docs before relying on either source for expiry behavior.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7749c215-285d-4345-aa0c-b03d3f78c1d8","uuid":"d921fd59-f5c5-42fc-9e6f-65b4ca98a287","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:34:08.523Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Intervals.icu API OAuth scopes ACTIVITY:READ CALENDAR:WRITE WELLNESS:READ refresh token expires_in","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015zzGwSVA7YsqJY1JKQD266","content":[{"title":"Intervals.icu OAuth support","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759"},{"title":"Überauth intervals.icu","url":"https://readme.hex.pm/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.0"},{"title":"Refresh the Access Token","url":"https://www.manageengine.com/appcreator/help/api/v2/refresh-the-access-token.html"},{"title":"docs.treedis.com","url":"https://docs.treedis.com/reference/models/OAuth2TokenData"},{"title":"OAuth Token Refresh","url":"https://developers.hellosign.com/docs/guides/o-auth/token-refresh"},{"title":"docs.privy.io","url":"https://docs.privy.io/reference/sdk/expo/interfaces/OAuthTokens"},{"title":"Name | Type | Description | Notes |","url":"https://github.com/UltraCart/rest_api_v2_sdk_php/blob/a5e19d4d9bff2beb9b827077fc3da23902e38fb2/docs/Model/OauthTokenResponse.md"},{"title":"Using Refresh Tokens","url":"https://docs.oracle.com/cd/F88966_01/English/Integration_Documentation/rest_api/D102899.html"},{"title":"Refresh the Access Token","url":"https://prezohoweb.zoho.com/creator/help/api/v2.1/refresh-the-access-token.html"}]},"The search turned up two Intervals.icu sources that address your question, and they don't fully agree on token expiry.\n\n- **Official forum post:** Scopes are ACTIVITY, WELLNESS, CALENDAR, CHATS, LIBRARY, and SETTINGS. Each needs READ or WRITE, and WRITE implies READ. The token exchange response includes an access token, granted scopes, and the athlete's id and name. That sample response has no `expires_in` or `refresh_token` field, and the post doesn't say anything about expiry.\n- **Community Ueberauth integration docs (hex.pm):** This source says the service departs from typical OAuth. Tokens do not expire, and there are no refresh tokens. It also describes CALENDAR as covering planned workouts and calendar events, and it describes WELLNESS as covering weight, HRV, resting HR, and sleep. Its default scope list is inconsistent: one passage gives ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:WRITE and another gives ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ.\n\nThe other results were about unrelated OAuth providers (ManageEngine, Zoho, Oracle, Treedis, HelloSign), so I've left them out. I found nothing confirming a `CALENDAR:WRITE` scope string as written, though the forum's scope format implies it is valid. I'd check the official Intervals.icu API docs before relying on either source for expiry behavior."],"durationSeconds":6.715229249999997,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Atx4x8vtnhV4xbLyBHpCVc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
