{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS7tucPshUCoo32uJzEa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the three bugs I could confirm in the code, and wrote the causes to `ANSWER.md`. The Intervals-side 400 is still open: I couldn't reach Intervals from here, so Connect will only fully work once that is resolved.\n\n**What was broken**\n1. **Connect always failed (every athlete).** The button was a plain link. Browser navigation doesn't send the `Authorization` header, so the server returned 401 before building the OAuth URL.\n2. **Authorize step returns 400 `invalid_request`.** This started when calendar scopes were added on 2026-10-02. The one connection made before then (Rivera) worked without them. The earlier test in the logs never removed the scope, so it doesn't rule scope out. I couldn't check the Intervals OAuth client's registration.\n3. **Connections expired after exactly one hour (Rivera).** Intervals' token response has no `expires_in` or `refresh_token`. The code defaulted to 3600s and then discarded the token.\n\n**What I changed**\n- `static/app.js` and `server.py`: the authorize step is now a `POST` that returns the URL. The SPA calls it with the token and then navigates there.\n- `server.py`: a token with no `expires_in` no longer expires. A 401 from Intervals on a wellness call now marks the connection for reconnect. The refresh path no longer crashes when `expires_in` is missing.\n- `config.py`: the client ID, secret, and scopes now read from the environment, falling back to the existing values. The deploy env was previously ignored.\n- **Scope decision:** `SCOPES` now defaults to the pre-calendar set, so Connect works. This turns calendar sync off by default. To turn it back on, set `INTERVALS_SCOPES` to include `CALENDAR:*`, after the OAuth client is enabled for calendar on Intervals' side. If you'd rather keep calendar in the default, the 400 has to be fixed on Intervals first.\n\n**Verification**\n- Both Python files compile and `app.js` passes `node --check`.\n- Locally: GET to the auth endpoint returns 404, POST without a token returns 401, and POST with a token returns the authorize URL.\n- A token with no expiry stays connected after simulating 10 hours.\n- Not tested: the real Intervals authorize, callback, and token exchange.\n\n**Noticed but not changed** (listed in `ANSWER.md`): the SPA falls back to the `tok-okafor` dev token when none is stored, disconnect doesn't revoke at Intervals, the refresher holds the lock during network calls, and state is in-memory only.\n\nNothing is committed, and nothing was sent to any external service. The one outside request was a web search for Intervals' scope and token documentation."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":172,"cache_read_input_tokens":52913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":172},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7749c215-285d-4345-aa0c-b03d3f78c1d8","uuid":"a365e673-0f75-446a-867c-4b7873dd4027","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:35:14.501Z","request_id":"req_011CgS7tuM1YQHCHMQxDqj7e"}
